' runtime.linux heap for programs compiled by the Fission native x86-64
' backend -- the allocator behind every string, array, object and (later)
' boxed dynamic value. Written in ArcoBASIC on top of MEMORY.Read64/Write64
' and LINUX.Syscall; compiled by the same backend as part of every native
' program (fission/cli/compile_to_x86_64.abas imports this module first, so
' its top-level initialization runs before user code).
'
' Memory comes from anonymous mmap in 64 MiB chunks (larger requests get a
' chunk of their own) and is handed out by a bump pointer, 16-byte aligned.
' Nothing is freed yet: reclaiming memory is separate, later work.
'
' Runtime locals are all rt-prefixed: a script-scope global is visible inside
' every FUNCTION that names it, so ordinary names here (`ignored`, `size`, ...)
' would silently alias a user program's own top-level variables.
'
' State lives in a small mmap'd page rather than in ArcoBASIC globals,
' because a script-scope global written inside a FUNCTION does not propagate
' (the language's copy-in semantics): FissionRt_HeapState holds the page's
' rtAddress, set once below; offset 0 = bump rtCursor, offset 8 = chunk rtLimit.

FUNCTION FissionRt_MapAnonymous(rtBytes)
    ' mmap(NULL, rtBytes, PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE, MAP_PRIVATE|MAP_ANONYMOUS, -1, 0)
    rtAddress = LINUX.Syscall(9, 0, rtBytes, 3, 34, -1, 0)
    IF rtAddress < 0 THEN
        ' Out of memory is fatal: report it, then exit_group(70).
        PRINT "Fission runtime: out of memory"
        rtIgnored = LINUX.Syscall(231, 70)
    END IF
    RETURN rtAddress
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION FissionRt_HeapInit()
    rtState = FissionRt_MapAnonymous(4096)
    rtIgnored = MEMORY.Write64(rtState, 0)
    rtIgnored = MEMORY.Write64(rtState + 8, 0)
    RETURN rtState
END FUNCTION

' Returns the rtAddress of `rtBytes` fresh rtBytes (zero-filled, since anonymous
' mappings are zero-filled and nothing is ever reused).

FissionRt_HeapState = FissionRt_HeapInit()
